# Line endings.
#
# `text=auto` lets git normalize text files to LF in the repository. The two
# explicit rules below also pin the working copy to LF on every platform,
# including Windows, because for these files the exact bytes matter:
#
#   *.sql  Migrations are hashed (packages/db/src/migrate.ts). A CRLF checkout
#          produces different checksums, and a checksum that disagrees with an
#          already-migrated database is a hard error that stops the migrate
#          step -- and therefore the API and the worker -- from starting.
#
#   *.sh   Shell scripts run inside Linux containers, where a CRLF line ending
#          makes bash fail with "\r: command not found".
* text=auto

*.sql text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
